.TH OPENKAL 1 "September 2026" "OpenKal" "Games"
.SH NAME
openkal \- start the OpenKal client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openkal
.SH DESCRIPTION
The first invocation creates
.I ~/.config/openkal/openkal.profile
from the packaged template and opens a folder picker. Select the KalOnline
client directory that contains the
.I data
and
.I map
directories. OpenKal validates the selected directory before it starts and
stores the resolved client paths in the profile. If validation fails, it asks
for a directory again. Canceling the picker exits without starting the client.
.PP
The embedded single-player server requires compatible world catalogs and area
maps. The project client package does not include a complete world. A locally
built package may include user-supplied world catalogs and area maps in
.IR /usr/share/openkal/config.pak .
.PP
Advanced users may edit that profile to set
.B data_root
and
.B map_root
to separate existing KalOnline asset directories. These paths are validated
before the client starts. Set
.B server_map_root
to use an external directory of compatible area maps.
.PP
User data, including the local SQLite state and UI settings, is stored in
.I ~/.local/share/openkal
by default. The XDG_CONFIG_HOME and XDG_DATA_HOME environment variables are
honored. Set OPENKAL_PROFILE to use a different profile path.
